From 3056405e0479330b0889c2a971452bfd10014b70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:10:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: stm32: move PMIC control to secure world in ST
 stm32mp15 boards

Move the control of the PMIC to the secure world (OP-TEE). Linux will
now rely on SCMI regulator and SCMI DVFS interfaces instead of directly
managing the PMIC.

Adopt PSCI power domains. The SCMI-related DT nodes have been factored out
into stm32mp15-scmi.dtsi so that all stm32mp15 SCMI boards benefit from
the common configuration.
LP-timer4 has been activated to allow PSCI OSI mode to work correctly.

Signed-off-by: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Iba2b3acfdc2de3eefceb56b1baf0376b31d3735a
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/593166
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
---
